Local fixes to reka-ui 2.11.0's built files. Drop each once upstream ships it.

1. CheckboxRoot, Radio, SwitchRoot: skip the `[for=id]` label lookup when the
   control already has `labels`, so rendering a control does not force a
   layout (storefront #206).

2. Dialogs no longer write `pointer-events: none` on <body> (storefront #156).
   Every element inherits it, so opening any modal dialog restyled the whole
   page inside the tap: 300-440 ms of a 750-880 ms phone-menu tap on a
   6x-slowed CPU, in both storefront designs. A dialog's overlay already
   catches a tap outside it. Upstream sources (v2.11.0) that write it:
   - packages/core/src/Dialog/DialogContentModal.vue:9
     `disableOutsidePointerEvents: true`, reaching
     packages/core/src/DismissableLayer/DismissableLayer.vue:178
     `acquireBodyPointerEvents(doc, element)`.
     Patched: the default is false.
   - packages/core/src/Dialog/DialogOverlayImpl.vue:19
     `useBodyScrollLock(props.present)`, reaching
     packages/core/src/shared/useBodyScrollLock.ts:89
     `acquireBodyPointerEvents(document, pointerEventsOwner)`.
     Patched: useBodyScrollLock takes `{ bodyPointerEvents: false }`, which
     DialogOverlayImpl passes. Menus, popovers, selects and comboboxes, which
     have no overlay, keep the write.
   Upstream: fixed on the reka-ui v3 branch by unovue/reka-ui#3070 (merged
   2026-10-27, unreleased on 2026-11-01): nothing there writes body
   pointer-events. Drop this part with the move to reka-ui v3.

